ips.format:
Each issue ships:
- 12-16 portrait stills;
- 6-second 9:16 loops;
- an issue page in the app and on the site, showing each look in stock at the member's home store;
- a WestStyleClub WhatsApp header;
- a printed issue card at every cash desk.
There are only two films per Mausam year: the Baarish issue film (a 45-60 second silent film) and the Five Functions series. Garmi is stills and loops only. The Dehleez 60-second piece is cut from the portrait sessions.

Each store has one bay holding one look family on 1-3 mannequins, from one own label a week in rotation (E.T.A., Utsa, Vark, Wardrobe, LOV, Nuon, Bombay Paisley). The look is built and photographed in one reference store and shipped on Tuesday as a VM kit sized for small mall bays; stores install it on Thursday night. Assets:
- one 3:4 still;
- a 6-second 9:16 loop;
- a WhatsApp header crop;
- the Google Business Profile photo;
- an A5 rail card with the number, the label and a QR code to HOLD.

ips.kpi:
Per store, per week:
- Friday-to-Sunday footfall in wave A stores against wave B stores, which install the same window a week later;
- HOLD requests and the share collected;
- seven-day Window-rail sell-through against the rest of the floor.

Per store and stylist:
- bookings and Style Calls from episodes and columns;
- show-up rate;
- share of booked visits that end in a bill, matched by WestStyleClub ID;
- average bill of booked visits against walk-ins at the same store;
- repeat bookings within 90 days.

Per new store:
- opening-week and day-30 footfall against the curve of comparable recent openings in the same city tier;
- RSVP attendance;
- new WestStyleClub members in the catchment;
- 30-day return rate (portrait collections and card redemptions);
- first-month sales against plan.

ips.format:
A numbered annual edition, made of:
- one artist's motif as a durable, anti-slip, mall-approved floor print at every store entrance;
- a small capsule across Utsa, Vark, Bombay Paisley and Studiowest, designed with the artist;
- a portrait studio at the threshold in 50 stores, run in off-peak hours by trained store teams;
- a 60-second film cut from the portrait sessions (30 families at 30 thresholds), with regional-language cuts.

ips.kpi:
Per store:
- portrait slots booked and attended;
- average family group size;
- bills from portrait families on the day;
- festive-period footfall like-for-like against Diwali 2026, the recorded baseline, read across the two install waves;
- capsule sell-through;
- posts geotagged to the store.

Per store:
- Bring the Card sessions, booked and walk-in;
- multi-function baskets (items per bill, and the share of bills above a set value);
- return visits to collect alterations;
- wedding-season footfall like-for-like against last season, for the pilot store and cluster against matched controls (with the January end-of-season sale matched in the controls);
- episode completion on WhatsApp.

Per creator and home store:
- member-attributed bills and new WestStyleClub sign-ups;
- share of stores with three or more active Regulars;
- store-tagged UGC (The Bench is scored on store-tagged posts and bills, not shares);
- runners checked in, and their bills within seven days.

naming_and_voice:
Number everything the same way:
- 'No. 047' for weekly and rolling series (three digits);
- 'No. 01' for Mausam issues;
- 'Edition 01' for annual moments;
- 'Episode 03' for films.
Numbers never restart. First Look follows Westside's store count once Trent confirms the rule.

